# Deliberately narrow: only the files where a CRLF is FATAL, not a whole-repo
# normalisation. `core.autocrlf=true` on a Windows checkout already keeps the
# repository itself LF, so rewriting every file's endings would be a huge diff
# that fixes nothing.
#
# These are different. A shell script committed with CRLF fails on Linux with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M" — the shebang line keeps the carriage return —
# and Docker reports it as a missing file, which sends you looking for a broken
# COPY instead of an invisible byte. Marking them here makes the guarantee a
# property of the repository rather than of whoever happens to clone it.
*.sh              text eol=lf
Dockerfile        text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Caddyfile         text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
*.yml             text eol=lf
*.yaml            text eol=lf
